Current implementation status

Steam is implemented in KubeJS as the first mechanical industrial age.
The Steam Engineering Core gates the first Create industrial toolkit:
Mechanical Press, Mechanical Mixer, Deployer, Mechanical Saw, Mechanical Drill, and Mechanical Crafter.

Steam → LV is implemented in KubeJS.
LV now requires GT steel, the Steam Engineering Core, a dedicated LV Machine Core, and a real GregTech Circuit Assembler recipe for Basic Electronic Circuits.

MV, HV, and EV are now implemented in KubeJS as explicit electrical progression gates.
MV requires aluminium, wrought iron, and a dedicated MV Machine Core; HV requires stainless steel, titanium, and a dedicated HV Machine Core; EV requires titanium, polyethylene, and a dedicated EV Machine Core.
Each tier replaces the stock GTCEu Machine Hull recipe so the tier transition is explicit.

IV, LuV, ZPM, and UV are now implemented in KubeJS as the next four electrical progression gates.
Each of these transitions consumes the previous tier's Machine Hull and introduces the corresponding high-tier materials and cabling.
UHV is now implemented as the final conventional electrical progression gate, consuming the UV Machine Hull and requiring extreme-tier materials.
Mekanism and AE2 integration remain intentionally gated until the electrical backbone is established.

